<article class="env-lemma" id="0GD6">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GD6">Lemma <span data-tag="0GD6">88.21.13</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of formal algebraic spaces. Assume that $X$ and $Y$ are locally Noetherian and $f$ is a closed immersion. The following are equivalent </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$f$ is rig-smooth and rig-surjective, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$f$ is rig-étale and rig-surjective, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
for every affine formal algebraic space $V$ and every morphism $V \to Y$ which is representable by algebraic spaces and étale the morphism $X \times _ Y V \to V$ corresponds to a surjective morphism $B \to A$ in $\textit{WAdm}^{Noeth}$ whose kernel $J$ has the following property: $IJ = 0$ for some ideal of definition $I$ of $B$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $I$ and $J$ be ideals of a ring $B$ such that $IJ^ n = 0$ and $I(J/J^2) = 0$. Then $I^ nJ = 0$ (proof omitted). Hence this lemma follows from a trivial combination of Lemmas <a href="/tag/0GD4" data-tag="0GD4">88.20.9</a> and <a href="/tag/0GD5" data-tag="0GD5">88.21.12</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>